  "prompt": "[system]\n\n    You generate compact, robust Python TSP metaheuristics.\n    You must follow the requested interface exactly, always preserve tour validity.\n    \n\n[user]\nPARENTS:\nCandidate cand_000020: rand_ils_sa_improved\n\nStatus: timeout; distance: 7.80909\n\nThought: Random-start nearest neighbor construction, then 2-opt local search, then iterated local search with double-bridge perturbation and simulated annealing acceptance (cooling temperature), and multiple restarts (5 runs) with increased SA iterations (30) to improve exploration and reduce tour distance.\n\nError details: timeout on tsp_construct_100_seed2024_001: Solver timed out after 30.0019s (timeout_seconds=30)\n\nCode:\n\n```python\n\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef solve_tsp(distance_matrix: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    n = len(distance_matrix)\n    best_tour = None\n    best_dist = np.inf\n\n    def two_opt(tour):\n        improved = True\n        while improved:\n            improved = False\n            for i in range(n - 2):\n                for j in range(i + 2, n):\n                    a, b = tour[i], tour[(i+1) % n]\n                    c, d = tour[j], tour[(j+1) % n]\n                    delta = (distance_matrix[a, c] + distance_matrix[b, d] - distance_matrix[a, b] - distance_matrix[c, d])\n                    if delta < -1e-12:\n                        tour[i+1:j+1] = np.flip(tour[i+1:j+1])\n                        improved = True\n                        break\n                if improved:\n                    break\n        return tour\n\n    def double_bridge(tour):\n        arr = tour.copy()\n        i, j, k, l = np.random.randint(0, n, 4)\n        a, b, c, d = sorted([i, j, k, l])\n        seg1 = arr[a:b]\n        seg2 = arr[b:c]\n        seg3 = arr[c:d]\n        seg4 = np.concatenate([arr[d:], arr[:a]])\n        return np.concatenate([seg1, seg4, seg3, seg2])\n\n    for restart in range(5):\n        # Random-start nearest neighbor\n        start = np.random.randint(n)